# PoC output. README documents exactly these two filenames
# (`npm run poc -- --json-output poc-chain-evidence.json --sarif-output
# poc-chain-evidence.sarif`), so anyone following the README produces them --
# they are a run artefact, not a deliverable, and neither was tracked nor
# ignored until now, which is one `git add -A` away from publishing them.
poc-chain-evidence.json
poc-chain-evidence.sarif
.npm-cache/

# External hunt targets + raw scan output: other people's repositories.
# NEVER commit to this public repo -- license/attribution, repo bloat, and
# which targets we scan is OPSEC-sensitive (README rule: no real target names).
# Only hunt/NOTES.md + hunt/README.md (generic, no target names) are trackable.
hunt/*
!hunt/NOTES.md
!hunt/README.md
